# Backend rules (future phase)

These rules apply only if/when a `backend/` Python service is added.
Current ResearchFlow phase uses Next.js API routes instead — do not create FastAPI
unless explicitly requested.

## Python style

- Type hints on every function signature and return value
- Async by default for API handlers and DB sessions
- No bare `except:`; raise domain exceptions with actionable messages
- Config/thresholds in settings, not magic numbers in logic

## FastAPI (when present)

- Thin route handlers: validate → service → response
- Services must not import FastAPI
- Declare `response_model=`; no raw ORM returns
- Long work (>2s) should become jobs with pollable status

## Security

- Never log API keys, full prompts with secrets, or raw uploaded file contents
- Parameterised SQL only
- Sanitize uploaded filenames; store under UUID paths

## Tests

- Happy-path + failure tests for services
- Mock AI provider calls in tests — no real LLM hits in CI
